<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>Operations Desk Dashboard Notes</title>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Operations Desk Dashboard</h1>
  <h2>Purpose</h2>
  <p>
    The Operations Desk dashboard provides a compact operating view of the incident and ticket backlog
    across planning and execution teams. It shows what is open, who owns it, how long items have been
    active, where escalation pressure is building, and how quickly issues are being closed.
  </p>

  <h2>What The Dashboard Shows</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Open Tickets, Escalations, Average Open Age, Average ETA, and Closed Items provide the top-line operating signal.</li>
    <li>Open and Closed Trend shows monthly intake, monthly closure, and the remaining open backlog.</li>
    <li>Issue Type Mix highlights where the current backlog is concentrated by category.</li>
    <li>Risk Snapshot isolates items that are blocked, aging, or critical.</li>
    <li>Open Incidents by Assignee shows workload concentration and average ticket age by owner.</li>
    <li>Backlog by Team shows open load and escalation pressure across NTT, o9, Anaplan, and Relex.</li>
    <li>Open Ticket Queue provides the working list with owner, status, priority, age, ETA, and latest update.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Key Highlights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The page is designed for daily operational review, not deep reporting.</li>
    <li>The layout keeps the most important questions visible first: how much is open, where risk is concentrated, who owns the work, and how quickly the backlog is moving.</li>
    <li>The queue is sorted priority-first so critical and older items stay visible.</li>
    <li>Current content uses seeded sample tickets and can later be connected to uploaded files or a ticket API.</li>
  </ul>
</body>
</html>
